 "text": "Hello! How are you doing these days? Glossy looks amazing for printed pictures, but it shows every fingerprint. Matte protects them, but the prints look softer. Then the prints will dry crisper in matte. If it's too warm, matte will be nicer. Then print the images just before the visit. It might be. A simple fan helps, or turn off the printer ten minutes before. Good thinking. Then matte for the photo books and a couple of warm prints on card. Good. Print the photos, then it' your call. Enjoy the visit.",
